# Day 2 - Linear Regression Using House Prices Dataset

## Objective

Build a Linear Regression model to predict house sale prices using house features from the Kaggle House Prices dataset.

## Dataset

* Dataset: House Prices - Advanced Regression Techniques
* Source: Kaggle
* File Used: train.csv

## Algorithm Used

* Linear Regression

## Feature and Target

### Feature (Input)

* GrLivArea (Above Ground Living Area)

### Target (Output)

* SalePrice

## Workflow

1. Load dataset using Pandas
2. Select feature and target variables
3. Split dataset into training and testing sets
4. Train Linear Regression model
5. Make predictions on test data
6. Evaluate model performance using R² Score and Mean Squared Error (MSE)
7. Predict the price of a new house

## Libraries Used

* Pandas
* Scikit-learn
* NumPy

## Evaluation Metrics

* R² Score
* Mean Squared Error (MSE)

## Concepts Learned

* Supervised Machine Learning
* Linear Regression
* Train-Test Split
* Model Training
* Prediction
* Model Evaluation

## Outcome

Successfully trained a Linear Regression model to predict house prices based on living area and evaluated its performance using standard regression metrics.
